# Minimal bootable Saphira image, systemd target.
#
# Intentions ONLY. The package manager owns dependency closure; never
# enumerate resolved dependencies here (saphira-profiles(5)).
#
# The minimum for a genuinely bootable, manageable machine, and nothing
# more. Each entry earns its place:
#
#   saphira-base        libc/loader, filesystem layout, apk, shell, core
#                       runtime, account and package tooling. The one
#                       existing Saphira group; the profile layers onto it
#                       rather than re-enumerating it.
#   saphira-kernel      the kernel and its modules. Boot is impossible
#                       without it.
#   systemd             the init system for this target.
#   grub                the bootloader. Deliberately an explicit
#                       intention: a bootable image carries its own
#                       bootloader, and later kernel upgrades need it.
#   e2fsprogs           mkfs.ext4 for the root filesystem.
#   openssh             login/access. A server with no remote access is
#                       not manageable.
#   iproute2            the `ip` tool (addresses, routes, links): named
#                       explicitly because no framework package pulls it
#                       in on systemd targets (see absent list).
#   vim                 the base editor. A headless server with no editor
#                       is not administrable.
#   procps-ng           process tools (ps, free, top): a working system
#                       needs a way to inspect processes and memory.
#   tzdata              a server with no timezone cannot reason about
#                       logs, certificates or scheduling.
#   kbd                 loadkeys/dumpkeys/kbd_mode: vconsole-setup execs
#                       /usr/bin/loadkeys at boot; without it the first
#                       console keeps the kernel keymap (proven Minimer
#                       2026-11-08). An image intention, not a systemd
#                       dependency: minimal hosts without a console still
#                       run the same init package.
#
# Deliberately absent, each a decision rather than an oversight:
#   - acpid: systemd-logind owns ACPI power-event handling on systemd
#     targets; a separate daemon would duplicate it. OpenRC has no
#     logind, so minimal-openrc carries acpid instead. A virsh
#     shutdown test must establish which component handled the event
#     before this is revisited.
#   - saphira-network + dhcpcd: the OpenRC network framework and its
#     DHCP client. systemd-networkd owns the NIC on systemd targets;
#     installing the framework alongside it is a conflicting network
#     stack, not a complement. Firstboot configures systemd targets
#     through networkd drop-ins directly.
#   - a graphical stack of any kind (see the headless policy);
#   - ca-certificates is already inside saphira-base;
#   - mail, DNS and web services: those are ROLE layers (see the
#     role-* profiles), not part of a minimal boot. vim is IN by
#     decision: a headless server with no editor is not administrable.
saphira-base
saphira-kernel-7.2.3
systemd
grub
e2fsprogs
openssh
iproute2
vim
procps-ng
tzdata
kbd
